 ## Overview
-A method to determine the target Gaussian population size for 3D Gaussian Splatting based on capture characteristics, specifically using track-adjusted pixels normalized against standard scenes, to replace fixed defaults [S1, unofficial]. It sets apart from sibling methods by ensuring the model budget is invariant to redundant views (e.g., duplicated images), whereas alternatives like total pixel count scale with view count and SfM point counts scale with matched-observation density rather than capture scale [S1, unofficial].
